>> Spellbook gifts can go to anyone with enough Luck; [...]

Numerical value of 8 is optimal for getting spellbooks when praying.  It
can take significant tracking to be certain of your current number - The
first time you see clovers at prayer a random number gets added to your
numerical luck.

> Aha, thanks. So it was also just luck that the gift had been
> a spellbook of magic missile. A clear divine hint to get some
> dragon scales as soon as possible to replace that mithril. :-)

There is a little bit more to it - At XP level N the game tries N times
to give you a book in a spell that you have not yet read in a school
that you know.  If that many tries fails then you get a completely
random book.

If your character class can only advance 2 schools, you're at a high
level, and you just started a sacrifest the chances of getting a spell
you want is high.  As you move towards knowing all of the spells in all
of your schools the chances of getting a random book starts to be higher
than finishing your schools.

Also it calculates based on books you have read.  Be sure to read a
blank book right away.  If you don't blank stays in the list of options.


